      - @ConditionalOnClass found required classes (matched)

Negative matches:
-----------------
   RedisAutoConfiguration:
      - @ConditionalOnClass did not find required class (did not match)
```

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- How does `@ConditionalOnMissingBean` know the order of bean registration? Auto-configuration classes are processed after user-defined `@Configuration` classes, so your beans are always registered first.
- Can you combine multiple conditional annotations on one bean? Yes. All conditions must be true for the bean to be created (they are combined with AND logic).
- How do you exclude a specific auto-configuration? Use `@SpringBootApplication(exclude = DataSourceAutoConfiguration.class)` or set `spring.autoconfigure.exclude` in properties.
- What is the difference between `@ConditionalOnProperty(matchIfMissing = true)` and `matchIfMissing = false`? With `matchIfMissing = true`, the bean is created even when the property is absent, making it opt-out. With `false` (default), the bean requires the property to exist.

```java
// Excluding a specific auto-configuration
@SpringBootApplication(exclude = DataSourceAutoConfiguration.class)
public class NationalBankBatchApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(NationalBankBatchApp.class, args);
    }
}
```
